1. OpenCV (https://github.com/opencv/opencv)

   The image processing kernels in src/ are ports to Zig of OpenCV source
   files: the algorithms, constants, tables and the order of arithmetic were
   taken from those files and rewritten in Zig. Each ported file carries a
   header naming its sources and stating that it was modified (translated to
   Zig, restructured around slices and the caller's allocator, and stripped
   of OpenCV's dispatch, OpenCL, IPP and HAL layers).

   OpenCV as a whole is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; a
   copy is in LICENSE-APACHE, as section 4(a) of that licence requires.
   Several of the ported files still carry OpenCV's earlier 3-clause BSD
   licence header; that header, with its copyright notice, conditions and
   disclaimer, is reproduced below as it requires.

